      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is more accurate to say the dissent strongly disagreed with *the very premise* of the majority opinion, not just the specific application of the \"history and tradition\" standard. The dissent argued that the right to abortion *is* a fundamental right, regardless of how the majority chose to define \"deeply rooted in this nation's history and tradition.\"\n\nTherefore, the conflict is one of fundamental constitutional interpretation: the majority prioritized the conservative understanding of historical precedent, while the dissent centered on the liberal view of evolving fundamental rights that pre-date such historical analysis in that specific context.",
